  "paragraphs": [
    "Iqa‘ Aqsaq is very popular in the Muwashah vocal genre. It is 1 beat short of Iqa‘ Sama‘i Thaqil but sometimes it can be played immediately before or after a piece in that iqa‘ without interruption, during a Wasla.",
    "An alternate form of Aqsaq replaces the rest on the 6the beat with another dum, thereby creating a sequence of 2 consecutive dum-s that evokes Iqa‘ Sama‘i Thaqil."
  ],
  "text": "Iqa‘ Aqsaq 9/8 Iqa‘ Index Pronunciation of Aqsaq Iqa‘ Aqsaq is very popular in the Muwashah vocal genre. It is 1 beat short of Iqa‘ Sama‘i Thaqil but sometimes it can be played immediately before or after a piece in that iqa‘ without interruption, during a Wasla. Muwashah Ma-htiyali Louis Hage & Aida Chalhoub Mouwashah - Chants Arabo-andalous Muwashah Ana Min Wajdi Ana Aicha Redouane Egypte Muwashah Jalla Man Bil Husni Sawwar Abdel Halim Noueira Ensemble Music by Kamel al-Khula‘i Muwashah el-Sama‘ wel-Rah Ibrahim el-Haggar Music by Dawud Husni Bashraf Bulbul al-Afrah Ensemble Morkos Iqa‘ Aqsaq 9/8 - Form I Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan The second form of Iqa‘ Aqsaq An alternate form of Aqsaq replaces the rest on the 6 the beat with another dum , thereby creating a sequence of 2 consecutive dum -s that evokes Iqa‘ Sama‘i Thaqil . Muwashah Ma-htiyali Al-Turath Ensemble The Music In Spanish Al Andalus - Hijaz Muwashah Ayyuha al-Saqi Sabah Fakhri Beiteddine Festival Vol. 1 Music by Majdi al-‘Aqili Muwashah ‘Adhibuni Ensemble Al-Kindi The Aleppian Music Room Vol. 1 - Hijazkar Kurd & Saba Music by ‘Umar al-Batsh Muwashah Bi Abi Bahi al-Jamal Muhammad Khayri (Syria) Iqa‘ Aqsaq 9/8 - Form II Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan",
